      "role": "user",
      "content": "wow, look at that score jump. the tool is definitely picking up on the extra detail. \n\nit's a lot more colorful, though i'm a tiny bit worried about some of the phrasing—like \"sun-blasted acidity\" or \"saccharine feast\" feels a little heavy-handed. that said, i get why the plugin likes it. \n\ncan we try one more pass to really nail the \"gourmet\" feel? i want the reader to feel like they are actually sitting in the restaurant. try to push the descriptive quality even further so we can get a top-tier richness score, but try to keep the flow natural. we want it to feel like high-end food journalism, not just a list of descriptors. focus on making the sensations—the smells, the textures, the atmosphere—incredibly lush and detailed.",
